<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43647" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĕnŏnes</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēnōnes</span></b> ,
			um, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σένονες</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σήνωνες</span>.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A people in</i> Gallia Lugdunensis, <i>whose chief city was</i> Agendicum, now <i>Sens</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 5, 54</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 56</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">6, 2</span></i> sq.; 6, 44; 7, 4 al.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 18,
				32, § 107</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 8,
			234</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 4, 160</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Eutr. 10, 7</span></i>.—In
				sing.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĕno</span></b> , ŏnis,
			m., <i>one of the Senones</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Drappeten Senonem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hirt. B. G. 8, 30</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A people in</i> Gallia Cisalpina, <i>sprung from the above</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 5,
			35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 26</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 15, 20, § 116</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĕnŏnĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Senones</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bellum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 17, 21, 21</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
